course: dictionary
lesson: 7280
title: Tiny words: the size of a pinhead
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A pinhead is the tiny round top of a pin. Writers use it to show that something is very, very small. When you read «the size of a pinhead», picture the tip of a pin and you know the thing is tiny.
explain: Context helps again. «Microbes are living things far too small to see; a thousand bacteria in a row would just about stretch across a pinhead.» The words far too small to see tell you the meaning before you reach pinhead. Try it: swap in "the tip of a pin" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Pinhead has a second, rude meaning. Calling someone a pinhead is slang for saying they are stupid, and it is an insult. The context shows which meaning is used: if it is about a person, it is the rude one. Do not use it about people, because it hurts their feelings.
explain: In science, a pinhead helps us compare sizes. A pinhead is about 1 to 2 millimetres across. «The varroa mite, about the size of a pinhead, feeds on bees» tells you the mite is tiny, and the comparison makes it easy to picture.
fact: A pinhead is the tiny round top of a pin.
fact: «The size of a pinhead» means very, very small.
fact: In science, a dot the size of a pinhead is about 1 to 2 millimetres across.
fact: As slang, «pinhead» is a rude insult meaning stupid, so never use it about people.
fact: «Plasma» carries red cells, white cells and platelets; a drop the size of a pinhead holds about 5 million red blood cells.
exercise: «The varroa mite, about the size of a pinhead, feeds on bees.» What does the size of a pinhead tell you? | Very loud | *Very small | Very large and heavy | Very old
exercise: Ella hears someone call her friend a pinhead. What does that mean? | It means a cold drink | It means the tiny top of a pin | It means very clever | *It is a rude insult meaning stupid
exercise: «A drop the size of a pinhead holds about 5 million red blood cells.» What does this show? | *A drop can be tiny but still hold a huge number of cells | Cells are bigger than a drop | Blood is always thick and sticky | Pins are used to take blood
test: «Bacteria in a row would just about stretch across a pinhead.» What does pinhead show here? | A kind of animal | *Something very small | A sharp needle for sewing | Something very large
test: A scientist measures a dot the size of a pinhead. About how wide is it? | About a kilometre across | About 10 metres across | About the weight of a bus | *About 1 to 2 millimetres across
exam: What is the rude meaning of pinhead? | Something very, very small | A kind of mite that feeds on bees | *Someone you think is stupid, said as an insult | The tiny round top of a pin
